[planner -> camera] PLAN REVIEW REQUEST — do NOT execute yet. Check only YOUR specialty (navigator / lidar / camera). Prefer ZERO tools; reply AGREE: or DISAGREE: in one line.

SPECIALIST PLAN:
Mission: Visit container first, then rock. Roles and assignments:

Navigator:
- Start from current pose. Repeat: stop at a safe free-cell goal, wait for sensors to finish, then follow new nav orders.
- If lidar reports a detected target object of the current tour class with centroid (x,y), compute a navigation goal at least 3.0 m from that centroid along the line toward the current robot pose (goal = centroid + 3*(pose - centroid)/||pose-centroid||) and navigate there and stop. Never navigate to an object centroid or closer than 3 m.
- If lidar reports no centroid for the current class after sensing, request an occupancy-based exploration goal: navigate to a nominated free cell (.) away from already-seen objects (pick a different quadrant) and stop.
- After stopping at a nav goal, await confirmation from lidar or camera before proceeding.

Lidar:
- When the robot is stopped, run semantic lidar scan and return any detected object centroids and class labels via get_semantic_lidar_objects.
- If you detect the current target class (container first, then rock), publish its centroid (x,y) immediately.
- After the navigator stops at a proposed visit pose for that class, call confirm_stop(class_name) to validate the stop.

Camera:
- When the robot is stopped, capture an RGB image and optionally provide a class histogram to assist identification.
- If lidar cannot confirm a stop, use camera and call confirm_stop(class_name) when appropriate.

Procedure / Rules:
1) Follow the ordered tour: container first, then rock. Do not skip order.
2) Use the sense → navigate → sense loop. Only sense when stopped.
3) Never send the navigator to a centroid or any goal closer than 3 m to an object.
4) After each stop at the target class, require confirm_stop(class_name) from lidar or camera. Do not proceed until confirm_stop returns true.
5) When a target class is not detected at current pose, use the occupancy map to pick a free '.' cell in a different quadrant from already-seen objects and navigate there, then sense again.
6) Report mission done only after both container and rock have been confirmed.

